CHAPTER V
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 8
Women and children victims of violence receive the following rights:
a. the right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected;
b. the right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by the victim;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality;
f. the right to compensation;
g. the right to social rehabilitation;
h. the right to complaint handling;
i. the right to assistance;
j. the right to obtain visum et repertum free of charge; and
k. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process.

CHAPTER III
SCOPE
Article 5
The scope of protection of women and children from violence, as follows: a. forms of violence against women and children;
b. rights of victims;
c. obligations and responsibilities;
d. implementation of protection of women and children from violence; e. institutions;
f. cooperation and partnership;
g. monitoring and evaluation;
h. reporting;
i. funding; and
j. Sanctions.

CHAPTER IV
FORMS OF VIOLENCE AGAINST WOMEN AND CHILDREN
Article 6
Forms of violence against women and children, among others:
a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. neglect;
e. exploitation; and/or
f. other violence.

Article 19
Forms of services for victims as referred to in Article 17 letter b, consist of:
a. services for women and children victims of acts of violence, including: 1. complaint, consultation and counseling services;
2. assistance services;
3. health services;
4. legal aid services; and
5. repatriation and social reintegration services.
b. special services for women victims of acts of domestic violence or human trafficking, including:
1. complaint services;
2. pick-up services;
3. medical and psychological referral services;
4. shelter services;
5. assistance and legal aid services; and 6. repatriation and social reintegration services.

CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES, PURPOSE AND OBJECTIVES
Article 2
Protection of women and children from violence is based on the principles of: a. humanity;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. protection;
d. best interests of women and children; and
e. non-discrimination.

REGENT OF GARUT
WEST JAVA PROVINCE
REGIONAL REGULATION OF GARUT REGENCY
NUMBER 13 OF 2016
CONCERNING
PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM VIOLENCE
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF GARUT,

Considering : a. that in order to guarantee and protect the rights of women and children so they can participate optimally in accordance with human dignity and honor, and receive protection from violence, it is necessary to undertake efforts to protect women and children optimally through increasing broad community participation;
b. that the prevalence of cases of violence against women and children in Garut Regency requires handling and concrete action from the Regional Government to formulate policies and programs to eliminate all forms of violence against women and children;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women and Children from Violence;

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 14 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Areas Within the Province of West Java (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1950 Number 8), as amended by Law Number 4 of 1968 concerning the Establishment of Purwakarta Regency and Subang Regency by Amending Law Number 14 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Areas Within the Province of West Java (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1968 Number 31, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 2851);
