e. non-discrimination.

Article 33
(1) The Sub-District Level Task Force for the Protection of Women and Children as referred to in Article 31 letter b, constitutes a functional work unit that provides integrated protection services and handling of cases of violence against children and women at the Sub-District level.
(2) The Management of the Sub-District Level Task Force for the Protection of Women and Children as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of:
a. elements of the Sub-District apparatus;
b. agencies/institutions at the Sub-District level;
c. elements of the Sector Police (Polsek);
d. elements of the Military District Command (Koramil);
e. community leaders/religious leaders;
f. youth elements; and
g. elements of the Sub-District PKK Driving Team.
(3) The main duties of the Sub-District Level Task Force for the Protection of Women and Children as referred to in paragraph (1) are:
a. providing services in the context of protecting women and children;
b. receiving public complaints regarding cases of violence against women and children in the Sub-District and Village areas;
c. facilitating women and children who are victims of violence in resolving their problems;
d. socializing to the community about the protection of women and children; and
e. providing assistance for victims or referring them to P2TP2A, Sector Police (Polsek)/Resort Police (Polres), hospitals or other institutions as required.
(4) Further provisions regarding the establishment, duties, and functions of the Sub-District Level Task Force for the Protection of Women and Children as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be stipulated by Decree of the Sub-District Head.

Article 4
The objectives of protection of women and children from violence are: a. to prevent violence against women and children;
b. to eliminate all forms of violence against women and children; c. to protect and provide a sense of security for women and children; d. to provide services to women and children victims of violence;
e. to carry out rehabilitation and reintegration of women and children victims of violence; and
f. to carry out empowerment of women and children victims of violence.

REGENT OF GARUT
WEST JAVA PROVINCE
REGIONAL REGULATION OF GARUT REGENCY
NUMBER 13 OF 2016
CONCERNING
PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM VIOLENCE
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF GARUT,

Considering : a. that in order to guarantee and protect the rights of women and children so they can participate optimally in accordance with human dignity and honor, and receive protection from violence, it is necessary to undertake efforts to protect women and children optimally through increasing broad community participation;
b. that the prevalence of cases of violence against women and children in Garut Regency requires handling and concrete action from the Regional Government to formulate policies and programs to eliminate all forms of violence against women and children;
