a. exchange of data and information;
b. rehabilitation of victims of violence;
c. repatriation and social reintegration;
d. provision of evidence and witnesses; and
e. empowerment.
(3) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall be set forth in the form of a Joint Agreement and/or Cooperation Agreement in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

